             mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000;
             padding:0 0 5px 0;">
<span style=3D"color:#000000 !important;text-decoration:none;">
      Why AI code review needs proof, not predictions
    </span>
</td>
</tr>
<!-- Body Text -->
<tr>
<td style=3D"font-family:Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:2=
2px;font-weight:normal;
               color:#000000 !important;mso-color-alt:windowtext;mso-style-=
textfill-fill-color:#000000;
               padding:0;">
<div style=3D"margin-top:0;">
<p>AI coding assistants can generate massive volumes of code in seconds, bu=
t when a text-only review misses a subtle runtime error, developers pay a m=
assive debugging tax, spending hours scraping logs, scrambling to reproduce=
 environments, and writing urgent hotfixes under pressure.</p>
<p>Greptile's new tool, <a href=3D"https://app.alphasignal.ai/c?uid=3DDhS8a=
jH7NeRZK5Ns&amp;cid=3D4f41ae2931bee134&amp;lid=3DjyacbXotASM16jum&amp;mid=
=3D5f6909b6-de1e-41c9-a0ee-f468f7ef0a68">TREX</a>, tackles this bottleneck =
by moving from static code analysis to active runtime execution.</p>
<p>TREX actively runs PR branches in a dynamic sandbox and automatically sp=
ins up dev servers, mocks API inputs, and executes interactions to catch fa=
ilures that static analysis cannot see.</p>
<p>By reading the code and then running it, <a href=3D"https://app.alphasig=
nal.ai/c?uid=3DDhS8ajH7NeRZK5Ns&amp;cid=3D4f41ae2931bee134&amp;lid=3Dnn564y=
6JGmGzbM6v&amp;mid=3D5f6909b6-de1e-41c9-a0ee-f468f7ef0a68">Greptile</a> mim=
ics the review and QA pipelines that real engineering teams build and autom=
ates the gruntwork of validation.</p>
<p>By executing the code during validation, TREX catches critical issues th=
at static analysis misses:</p>
<ul>
<li>Runtime bugs like the application inexplicably freezing two seconds int=
o startup.</li>
<li>Complex security vulnerabilities, like a shell expansion bypass that qu=
ietly leaks secrets.</li>
</ul>
<p><b>The ceiling of static analysis</b></p>
<p>Though large language models have gotten much better at finding bugs and=
 reasoning about code logic, they still struggle to predict complex runtime=
 state failures.</p>
<p>These are issues caused by dynamic memory mutations, asynchronous event =
loops, race conditions, or stateful database connection pools that happen d=
uring code execution.</p>
<p>This is exactly what creates the debugging tax. A text-only AI reviewer =
will frequently approve a PR where the TypeScript types and function logic =
look clean in isolation. However, in production, an edge-case null payload =
passing through an async middleware chain triggers an unhandled promise rej=
ection and a 500 server error.</p>
<p>When a bug like this slips past review, the team is forced into damage c=
ontrol: bisecting git commits, scraping distributed log aggregators, and pa=
tching the logic under immense pressure.</p>
<p>Safely scaling AI code generation requires an evolutionary leap in QA. T=
eams need to shift from passive compute prediction to active code execution=
. Active execution requires the AI to actually compile, execute, and evalua=
te the software in an isolated environment.</p>
<p>Instead of an LLM passively guessing that a database query might time ou=
t if a user ID is null, active code execution spins up an ephemeral contain=
er. It fires a payload against the live endpoint, measures execution, and i=
ntercepts the real HTTP 504 log directly.</p>
<p><b>TREX runtime validation and proof of work</b></p>
<p>Attempting to make a single AI agent run services, take screenshots, and=
 run tests can overload the model's context window.</p>
<img alt=3D"alpha_signal_image_1" border=3D"0" src=3D"https://alphasignal.a=
i/image/1785576117298-58vao4.png" style=3D"display:block;width:100%;max-wid=
th:560px;height:auto;" width=3D"560"/>
<p>To keep the context focused, the main Greptile reviewer acts as an orche=
strator. When it reads a diff and identifies an issue, it spins up a dedica=
ted TREX sub-agent scoped exclusively to investigate that specific problem =
in an isolated sandbox.</p>
<p>Take a new UI component hidden behind an authentication gate as an examp=
le. Testing this locally normally requires setting up the dev environment, =
handling web tokens, and manually toggling feature flags.</p>
<p>A TREX sub-agent figures this all out autonomously. It interacts with th=
e app and returns to the PR with a screenshot of the rendered feature that =
shows whether it works or breaks.</p>
<p>An AI that only leaves a text comment reading "this might fail" creates =
more work. The developer still has to pull the branch, start the server, an=
d verify the results.</p>
<p>By attaching concrete artifacts to the PR, TREX ensures the developer ne=
ver has to run the code themselves.</p>
<p><b>Under the hood: the semantic code graph and continuous learning</b></=
p>
<p>Executing code in a sandbox sounds simple, but running blind tests on a =
complex codebase is computationally impossible. Before TREX can execute a s=
ingle test, it needs to know what to test.</p>
<img alt=3D"alpha_signal_image_2" border=3D"0" src=3D"https://alphasignal.a=
i/image/1785576144466-s8pf0y.png" style=3D"display:block;width:100%;max-wid=
th:560px;height:auto;" width=3D"560"/>
<p>That context comes from Greptile's underlying <a href=3D"https://app.alp=
hasignal.ai/c?uid=3DDhS8ajH7NeRZK5Ns&amp;cid=3D4f41ae2931bee134&amp;lid=3D1=
tPAfBxrrKBEhTaeB&amp;mid=3D5f6909b6-de1e-41c9-a0ee-f468f7ef0a68">Semantic C=
ode Graph</a>. Before running any code, Greptile parses the entire reposito=
ry to extract and map directories, files, functions, variables, and classes=
.</p>
<p>When a PR is submitted, Greptile acts as an orchestrator. It deploys a s=
warm of parallel AI agents that query the graph index to trace dependencies=
 and assess impact well beyond the changed lines.</p>
<p>However, mapping static code isn't enough on its own. Greptile continuou=
sly learns and adapts to the team's undocumented preferences and engineerin=
g standards.</p>
<p>By ingesting internal documentation and reading historical and ongoing P=
R comments, the system dynamically adapts its custom rules over time. This =
leads to highly tailored reviews that understand the nuances of your specif=
ic stack.</p>
<p>This combination of deep codebase mapping and continuous cultural learni=
ng is why Greptile's core reading layer catches the subtle issues that diff=
-only AI tools miss:</p>
<ul>
<li>Cross-service logical bugs</li>
<li>Silent exception swallowing</li>
<li>Stylistic regressions</li>
</ul>
<p><b>The central validation layer: Greptile CLI and the `/greploop`</b></p=
>
<p>Greptile allows you to get the rigorous code auditing without leaving yo=
ur existing workflows.</p>
<p>Developers don't have to wait for a GitHub PR to get codebase-aware feed=
back. The <a href=3D"https://app.alphasignal.ai/c?uid=3DDhS8ajH7NeRZK5Ns&am=
p;cid=3D4f41ae2931bee134&amp;lid=3D7lWwLM66sWKn3KkY&amp;mid=3D5f6909b6-de1e=
-41c9-a0ee-f468f7ef0a68">Greptile CLI</a> allows engineers to run a full re=
pository review locally in the terminal.</p>
<p>The CLI includes an "--agent" mode that lets your local coding assistant=
s trigger Greptile themselves. They receive findings and suggested fixes as=
 raw text to iterate on immediately.</p>
<p>For ultimate autonomy, the "/greploop" skill creates a self-healing deve=
loper loop that follows a five-step cycle:</p>
<ul>
<li>An AI agent writes code</li>
<li>It triggers a Greptile review</li>
<li>The agent reads the resulting feedback</li>
<li>It applies the exact fixes and pushes the commit</li>
<li>It triggers another review</li>
</ul>
<p>The system repeats the loop up to five times to prevent runaway cycles. =
It continues until Greptile scores the PR a perfect five out of five with z=
ero unresolved comments.</p>
<p><b>Real-world impact</b></p>
<p><a href=3D"https://app.alphasignal.ai/c?uid=3DDhS8ajH7NeRZK5Ns&amp;cid=
=3D4f41ae2931bee134&amp;lid=3DQ3Jxwe51tsyUbom1&amp;mid=3D5f6909b6-de1e-41c9=
-a0ee-f468f7ef0a68">Brex integrated Greptile</a> to navigate their massive,=
 8-year-old monorepo with high precision and low noise. By catching what hu=
man reviewers easily miss, the platform helped Brex ship features 30% faste=
r. CTO James Reggio officially called it "the only AI reviewer that doesn't=
 annoy the s**t out of me."</p>
<p>We can also see TREX runtime validation <a href=3D"https://app.alphasign=
al.ai/c?uid=3DDhS8ajH7NeRZK5Ns&amp;cid=3D4f41ae2931bee134&amp;lid=3D1A8biz4=
zK2yLcnSry&amp;mid=3D5f6909b6-de1e-41c9-a0ee-f468f7ef0a68">catching bugs in=
 the wild</a>. In the "workos/oagen" repository, Greptile caught a correctn=
ess bug leaking sibling models and breaking a selected-only contract.</p>
<p>More critically, in the "hashgraph-online/hol-guard" repository, it iden=
tified a severe vulnerability where a shell expansion bypass allowed secret=
s to exfiltrate past a kubectl guard.</p>
<p>Crucially, TREX didn't just leave a text warning about the security flaw=
. It actively spun up a sandbox, executed the malicious payload, fired it a=
gainst the logic, and attached the exact failure output as proof of work di=
rectly in the PR.</p>
<p>Greptile's benchmarks show that teams relying on this automated validati=
on layer merge pull requests up to 4x faster and catch 3x more production-b=
locking bugs than those relying on static review alone.</p>
<p><b>Enterprise-scale deployment</b></p>
<p>To support large-scale engineering teams, Greptile also offers self-host=
ed, air-gapped deployments. Organizations can deploy the system entirely wi=
thin their own virtual private cloud to maintain strict data residency requ=
irements.</p>
<p>The platform is SOC 2 Type II compliant and includes standard enterprise=
 controls like SSO and comprehensive audit logs.</p>
<p>AI code generation is only as fast as your validation pipeline. Relying =
on manual human testing to validate AI-generated code nullifies the velocit=
y gains of using AI in the first place.</p>
<p>You can begin a <a href=3D"https://app.alphasignal.ai/c?uid=3DDhS8ajH7Ne=
RZK5Ns&amp;cid=3D4f41ae2931bee134&amp;lid=3Dnn564y6JGmGzbM6v&amp;mid=3D5f69=
09b6-de1e-41c9-a0ee-f468f7ef0a68">14-day free trial</a> to experience the a=
utomated validation layer against your own codebases.</p>
</div>
